      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Based on your settings, one possible reason for the patchy and faded spots is that the heat press temperature might be too low. Polyester fabrics typically have a lower thermal diffusivity than other materials, meaning they can absorb heat unevenly and lead to cooling faster, resulting in incomplete curing of the sublimation ink. Increasing the temperature or adjusting the dwell time may help improve color transfer.",
